# 2brain:start — regenerate with: 2brain <repo-path>
# .graphifyignore — graphify's scan-exclusion list: gitignore syntax, one
# pattern per line, read alongside .gitignore to decide which files get
# extracted into the code graph.
#
# The directories below hold 2brain's own generated documentation. They are
# not gitignored (they are committed on purpose), so without this file
# graphify would extract generated prose back into the next graph.
.2brain/
# 2brain:end

# --- hand-maintained (outside the 2brain block, preserved across runs) ---
# Planning prose is not topology. graphify extracts these as concept nodes:
# the 2026-09-13 run made "2brain Improvement Plan (Master)" the single most
# connected node in the repo (36 edges), pushed the node count over
# REPO_GRAPH_CLUSTER_MIN_NODES so GRAPH_REPORT.md was generated, and fed plan
# filenames into per-file page prompts as if they were dependencies. Kept as
# standing policy — the directory is empty today, and this makes it safe to
# fill again. Paired with the same exclusion in .2brainignore, which governs
# what 2brain documents rather than what graphify extracts.
docs/plans/
